Cell["6. Cancellation-factor families and boundary closures", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f8696be7-fd30-4055-b721-ec3f7832f02e"],

Cell["\<\
Across the 13 staged candidates, the number of cancellation factors per \
candidate has profile <|2 -> 13|>. Part I returns one generator per \
candidate; in these samples each generator factors into two of the reported \
cancellation factors. After canonicalising overall signs and normalisations, \
there are 8 distinct cancellation-factor polynomials and 7 distinct product \
generators. The identity of the factor set or generator is therefore a useful \
family label; the factor count alone need not be.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8535c459-9724-48a6-8280-92286674a371"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"factorGroups", "=", 
   RowBox[{"GatherBy", "[", 
    RowBox[{"factorRecords", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<FactorKey\>\"", "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"generatorGroups", "=", 
   RowBox[{"GatherBy", "[", 
    RowBox[{"generatorRecords", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<GeneratorKey\>\"", "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"KeyTake", "[", 
   RowBox[{"auditSummary", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<DistinctCancellationFactorCount\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<DistinctGeneratorCount\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<PullbackVectorsSharedAcrossGeneratorFamilies\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<BoundaryVectorsWithInteriorExtension\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<BoundaryVectorsWithoutInteriorExtension\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cfb6b502-1b15-47f4-be5c-28802a510d22"],

